From 851e72eed448a002074ad3b4ed8f2462d7078f2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:34:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sessions): outcome refresh on notices and card moves,
 notice guarantee, fan-out filter, restart and draft repairs [daveey]

Session-outcome contract, core behavior (lane A2):
- A kanban notice row written by the live poller, the unloaded sweeper or the remote sweep refreshes the
  chat's stored outcome (trigger notice).
- card_change_pass (unloaded sweeper loop) reads each board's status events, refreshes every linked chat
  (trigger card_change) and marks the card's earlier "blocked" notices display_metadata.stale once it
  leaves blocked.
- Notice guarantee: a chat ending on a kanban notice older than 5 min with no live turn gets ONE close-out
  wake (notice row claimed by CAS, 2 started per hour per lineage, chats held by another backend left to
  it); a notice about a card blocked on a human never wakes and refreshes to decision; a refused wake or a
  spent budget refreshes to unresolved{notice_tail}.
- Fan-out: no notice or card-change refresh for released links, archived chats or moved_to_gateway copies.
- desktop.auto_continue.resume_on_startup defaults on: boot continues fresh interrupted turns nobody reopens.
- The orphan reap tells a parent chat when its subagent was killed mid-work (unresolved{subagent_killed}).
- Maintenance archives interactive drafts with no message older than 24 h (hourly, any auto_archive setting).
- kanban human_request accepts optional choices: 2-6 {label, value}.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
